# What CAPNICo authenticates to the NICo API with.
#
# The name and namespace are not configurable: CAPNICo's own defaults read
# `nico-credentials` in `capnico-system`, and the keys below are what its
# config expects. Applied BEFORE the controller. The controller reads the
# Secret on each reconcile, so a change to it takes effect without a restart.
#
# Two forms, and CAPNICo refuses a Secret carrying both. A static `token` is
# what a substrate with issued credentials uses -- Forge's is an API key. The
# OAuth client is for a substrate that mints: the token a mint returns expires
# (fifteen minutes on DSX) and nothing refreshes this Secret, so a site given
# one stops being able to create machines long before it stops running. Handed
# the client instead, CAPNICo mints its own and keeps minting.
#
# The branch is on `tokenURL` rather than on `token` because it has to be
# decidable without any credential at all: an external render deliberately
# holds none, so a condition on the secret would read every site as the OAuth
# one and tell the operator to supply the wrong fields. The token URL is
# configuration -- which issuer this site mints from -- and so is present
# exactly when the OAuth form is the one in use.
#
# On this path the endpoint is the real NICo API -- https://api.ngc.nvidia.com
# on a real site -- and the token is a live API key, which is why
# this is a template item and not a committed manifest.
#
# It is the ONLY difference between this and the nico-sim lane: same provider,
# same CRDs, same controller, a different endpoint. That is what makes a green
# capnico-e2e run evidence about this path rather than a separate claim.
#
# Until an instance is actually created, `nvkectl get providers` reporting
# CONFIGURED means only that this Secret exists, not that it authenticates.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: nico-credentials
  namespace: capnico-system
type: Opaque
stringData:
  endpoint: "{{ .Nico.Endpoint }}"
  orgID: "{{ .Nico.OrgID }}"
  apiName: "{{ .Nico.APIName }}"
{{- if .Nico.TokenURL }}
  tokenURL: "{{ .Nico.TokenURL }}"
  clientID: "{{ .Nico.ClientID }}"
  clientSecret: "{{ .Nico.ClientSecret }}"
  scope: "{{ .Nico.Scope }}"
{{- else }}
  token: "{{ .Nico.Token }}"
{{- end }}
